{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791697324,"nonce":"A0Q+D4nP6SBm2eHyFiOENhj7QLA=","title":"A div of prose was laid out as a line for each of its pieces","message":"A div holding text, a code element and more text (a note on the wiki) showed each piece on a line of its own: only the paragraph tags (p, li, td and the like) made a flow of inline content, and every other element is a flex container by default.\n\nFix: any element that is not a control, a list or a table part, and not itself inline, is a flow when it holds text beside an inline element or more text. A row of spans or controls, with no text of its own, is still a row. tests/native-inline-flow.mjs has a div and a p of the same words and requires the same height, and a row of spans staying side by side.\n\nAlso in this change: a textarea has a default width, as the other fields do, so it does not shrink to its text in a shrink-wrapped parent, and it never scrolls sideways.","files":null}]}